Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-105: Up / Down in a number field, like Blend's
 (0.105.0)

Blend's number fields step with the arrow keys. Here Up / Down in Left / Top /
Width / Height / Font.Size only changed the number; it was written when the field
was left, and each change was its own undo step. Now Up / Down = +1 / -1 (Shift
= 10) at once in the field, and the edit is written when the keys stop (0.4 s),
on Enter or on leaving the field -- a run of presses is ONE edit, one Ctrl+Z; a
value already sent is not sent again.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 162, smoke 187, panels, real VS Code 159):
panels (Top 8 -> Up x3, Shift+Up, Down = 20 at once, nothing sent while
pressing, ONE setLayout top 20 on leaving it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
